notes: Wave 1. README still says the control sits in front of drones, robots and machine-learning pipelines as if those runtimes shipped. The worked scene is aep-live-entry. Domain subprotocols are attach examples. The kernel sequence is seal, freeze, wait, collect-all Admit then Apply. TypeScript processEvent is not product Admit and that law already lives in one-live-entry-language plus source_invariants. AEP-SDKs README labels every language Operational. Double-check of the clients: TypeScript aep-protocol is a thin lattice client. TypeScript dynAEP is a standalone component and not product Admit. Python aep-protocol and dynaep are source-only thin clients with no pip registry. Elixir shells out to aep-lattice-log. Go BuildLatticeFrame shells out to aep-lattice-log. Rust SDK is helper crates rather than an in-process sealer. Astro, Vue and html-css are stubs or tokens. Publish one maturity table in README and in AEP-SDKs README with classes native sealer, thin client, source-only thin client, placeholder and not product Admit. Classify each row by the code rather than by an Operational slogan. Do not add a drone runtime. Do not claim a language client is a native sealer when it shells out to aep-lattice-log. Do not treat TypeScript processEvent as product Admit.
acceptance: README no longer names drones, robots or machine-learning pipelines as shipped surfaces. README states one kernel sequence with live-entry as the worked scene and subprotocols as attach examples. README and AEP-SDKs README share one maturity table. Elixir and Go are thin client. Python is source-only thin client. TypeScript dynAEP is not product Admit. html-css, Astro and Vue are not Operational. source_invariants fails if AEP-SDKs README still says Operational for elixir, go, python, html-css, astro or vue. source_invariants fails if README still names drones or robots as shipped surfaces. cargo test -p aep-base-node --test source_invariants passes after the copy. scripts/gate-aep28-env-077.sh runs that test. nla-policy-scan gate coding-completion and project-completion-bac on AEP-Base-Node crate.
